            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Memetics and Cultural Evolution</strong><br>\nIn \"The Selfish Gene,\" Dawkins also introduced the concept of the meme, which parallels the idea of genes but in the realm of cultural evolution. Memes are units of cultural information, like tunes, ideas, or catch-phrases, that replicate and spread among people. This theory has sparked debate and further study on how cultural evolution parallels and diverges from biological evolution.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Blind Watchmaker</strong><br>\nDawkins continued to explore evolutionary concepts in his 1986 book, \"The Blind Watchmaker.\" He argues against the watchmaker analogy, a traditional argument for the existence of God, by asserting that natural selection can explain complex biological features without the need for an intelligent designer. The book is celebrated for its explanation of evolution as a blind, automatic, and non-purposive process.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Criticism of Creationism</strong><br>\nA vocal critic of creationism and intelligent design, Dawkins has been a prominent figure in public debates regarding science and religion. He argues that creationism is a myth and not supported by evidence, and he is concerned about its presence in educational systems. Dawkins believes that understanding evolution is crucial to biology and that supernatural explanations hinder scientific progress.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
